            <ArticleTitle>Salmonella myocarditis presenting as acute myocardial infarction: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>602-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac involvement with Salmonella infection is well known and electrocardiographic changes bear a direct relationship to prognosis. We present here a case with ECG changes mimicking an acute myocardial infarction in salmonella infection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
